    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1c102fbf8c8a54851884256aa6d497ccd024cbdff111f3e3efc09546cd6425f5",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Test regularity changes the discrepancy mechanism available to the source: repeated integration by parts converts smooth compact support into rapid vertical-strip Mellin decay suitable for contour estimates, while interval indicators expose discrete totient jumps; a prime-step recurrence then contradicts any overly fast remainder for those rough tests. The introductory Poisson example gives the analogous regularity-to-transform-decay pattern in an additive comparison family.",
