    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9a65a79df64fd3ce68debd2375c43bec028c8fbc7fbea94bf7b360ab389d85d4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The designated test F trades generic smooth-test regularity for pole transparency: its Mellin transform is stated to have, in the relevant half-plane, only poles contributed by zeta zeros. Although it is not of Paley-Wiener type, its weaker decay and derivative control still support a rectangle shift and a Fourier representation in log y, so a hypothetical gap between the rightmost zeros and Re(s)=1 forces remainder decay incompatible with F's extreme-discrepancy condition.",
