    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9fbb2cca399b88809fcf50936e430bb1ab772730738bb996879223b7a995747b",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source links universal measure-convergence rates to zero-free regions through Mellin analysis: the test-dependent entire factor separates from a meromorphic zeta factor, zeta estimates permit inversion-line movement, and the converse turns a universal rate into half-plane holomorphy while choosing a test nonvanishing at a proposed zero prevents accidental cancellation. The rightmost-zero abscissa thereby becomes a boundary for the attainable rate hierarchy.",
